---
title: "4 · Template details and saving"
description: Set the default case length and the client requirement, and save a new version of the template.
sidebar:
  order: 5
  label: "4 · Template details and saving"
---

**Who:** tenant admin, or a user with **Template access**. **Where:** the template editor.

## Details

On the **Details** tab, under **Template settings**, set **Default case length**, for example `10` business days. **Needs a client** is on by default: a client must then be chosen when a case is started from the template.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/details-settings" caption="The Details tab." /%}

## Unsaved changes

While the template has unsaved changes, **Discard** and **Save changes** are shown at the top right.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/editor-unsaved" caption="Discard and Save changes at the top right." /%}

## If saving is refused

When you save, Operon checks the template. If something must be corrected, the save is refused and a list of the problems opens at the top of the editor. Select a group in the list to read what to correct. The most common reasons are:

- If a task is due relative to the case due date, **Default case length** must be set on the **Details** tab.
- A section that has **Moves the case forward** turned on needs a **Board status**.
- At least one task must have **Must be done** turned on.

Each problem names the section or task to correct.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/save-refused" caption="A save refused, with the item to correct." /%}

## Saved

After you select **Save changes**, the status shows **Saved** and the version goes up by one (for example **v3**). Cases that have already started keep the version that they started with.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/editor-saved" caption="The template saved as a new version." /%}
